CiukiOS: JavaScript heap and thread setup that cannot end the browser. G26B
charges Duktape allocations to the JavaScript budget (port/js_memory.c, an
eighth of free memory). Upstream js_newheap and js_newthread build the
prototypes, thread map and window object without a catchpoint, so a refused
allocation ended in Duktape's default fatal handler (abort) or, when the
uncaught-error text could not be allocated either, in unbounded recursion
(stack overflow); the generated dukky_create_prototypes() skips a prototype
whose allocation failed, and a missing Window prototype made the window an
HTMLUnknownElement over the browser_window pointer (crash in its finaliser).
Now: a heap is made only with 1 MiB of budget left, setup steps run under
duk_safe_call, a refused allocation during heap setup discards the heap, and
a document whose thread failed is not retried at every inserted element. A
window without a heap has no scripting (NULL heap and thread, as with the
"none" backend) and one stderr line, instead of no browser. At process exit
(port/js_memory.h ciuki_js_exiting, set by the exit report) the target does
not tear the Duktape heap down: the OS reclaims the process, and the teardown
overflowed the 1 MiB main stack at every close (QEMU 2026-10-25).

